// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Fortunata 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1645040801" "Fortunatas are female Arachnos agents gifted with psychic powers. Those with aggressive abilities are tasked with taking down super-types-who often have little resistance to their deadly abilities."
// DisplayNames :
"P386767672" "Rogue Fortunata"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Fortunata_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Fortunata_Mistress 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3616015803" "The most powerful of the Fortunats are the Mistresses. These rare few have mastered numerous psychic abilities and risen to the top of Lord Recluse's beautiful Black Widows."
// DisplayNames :
"P2476311430" "Rogue Fortunata Mistress"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Fortunata_Mistress_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Crab_Spider 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3955054325" "Crab Spiders function much like SWAT teams in other cities, and are dispatched to deal with high-level threats like super-types. They're equipped with full body armor, larger weapons, and a set of mechanical spider arms that turn them into death-dealing machines."
// DisplayNames :
"P2327647566" "Rogue Crab Spider Slicer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Crab_Spider_Venomator 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P443920725" "Rogue Crab Spider Longfang"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Crab_Spider_Venomator_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Crab_Spider_Chief 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3318456577" "Rogue Crab Spider Webmaster"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Crab_Spider_Chief_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Mu_Striker 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P618109883" "Strikers are descendents of the long-lost Mu, drafted into Arachnos service to fight both mystic heroes and the troublesome Circle of Thorns."
// DisplayNames :
"P1088760489" "Rogue Mu Striker"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Mu_Striker_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Mu_Adept_Low 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P685380384" "The most gifted Mu Strikers are given far more than promotions and new uniforms-they are given eldritch secrets to unlock their inner powers. As long as they continue to use them in Arachnos' service, of course."
// DisplayNames :
"P3022370318" "Rogue Mu Adept"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Mu_Adept 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Mu_Adept_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Mu_Guardian_Low 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1655972707" "Mu Guardians pulse with the blood of their slaughtered ancestors in their veins. They have read unholy tomes, visited other planes of existence, and performed dark sacrifices too terrible to mention to become masters of the mystic arts."
// DisplayNames :
"P723523543" "Rogue Mu Guardian"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Mu_Guardian 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Mu_Guardian_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Spiderling 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P22379172" "These attack drones are used to soften up super-powered targets. Arachnos considers them very expendable, and uses them to record and monitor a threat's abilities before more expensive troops-such as Tarantulas or Fortunatas-are deployed."
// DisplayNames :
"P452613349" "Rogue Spiderling"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Tarantula_Low 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P498389093" "The Tarantula Exoskeleton Armor was developed by an Orb Weaver cell named Weaver One. It grants the user incredible strength and wires him directly to his weapons systems. Rumor is that the pilot must undergo a terrible treatment of some sort to properly graft with the suit."
// DisplayNames :
"P1644884552" "Rogue Tarantula"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Tarantula_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Fire_Tarantula 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P463381167" "Rogue Fire Tarantula"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Tarantula_Mistress_Low 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P792976714" "A rare few Fortunatas volunteer for the Tarantula program. Those who survive integration with the machine are truly terrors to behold. Their specially-designed suits greatly amplify their psychic abilities, allowing them to to not only communicate the next few seconds of time to their allies, but also to distort reality for their foes as well."
// DisplayNames :
"P852908351" "Rogue Tarantula Mistress"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Tarantula_Mistress_High 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Toxic_Tarantula_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P821625724" "Rogue Toxic Tarantula"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Tarantula_Queen 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3633229149" "What terrible process pushes a woman to become one of these unholy terrors is a subject of much speculation. What is known is that their suits are little different from Tarantula Mistresses. Instead, it seems the user somehow suffers the upgrade. Tarantula Queens are all incredibly powerful, but also quite mad."
// DisplayNames :
"P3866213408" "Rogue Tarantula Queen"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Dual_Turret 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3603313452" "Turrets like these are rumored to be based on designs stolen (or bought) from Crey industries. This one matches the design for a Dual Artillery Gun. The Crey security catalog entry reads: 'Our Dual Artillery Gun provides an excellent balance between the need for concentrated firepower and the desire to keep under budget. Ask about our options close-quarter flamethrower!'"
// DisplayNames :
"P1044660750" "Rogue Dual Artillery Gun"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Quad_Turret 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1213718413" "Turrets like these are rumored to be based on designs stolen (or bought) from Crey industries. This one matches the design for a Quad Howitzer Battery. The Crey security catalog entry reads: 'The Quad Howitzer Battery provides top-notch firepower for defending your installation with its four heavy cannons and optional flamethrower.'"
// DisplayNames :
"P1026236999" "Rogue Quad Howitzer Battery"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Frag_Missile_Turret 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3531456655" "Turrets like these are rumored to be based on designs stolen (or bought) from Crey industries. This one matches the design for a High-Explosive Missile Turret. The Crey security catalog entry reads: 'When you need maximum defense and cost is no concern, the Hi-Explosive Missile Turret is the premier choice. It's high-powered explosive rockets can ruin the day for nearly any attacker.'"
// DisplayNames :
"P2410410972" "Rogue High-Explosive Missile Turret"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Marshall_Blitz_Stage1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2079812247" "Marshal Jason Blitz used to be the Arachnos Marshal for the isle of Warburg, one of the western-most Rogue Isles, and is today the de facto ruler of it. Marshal Blitz commands a contingent of Rogue Arachnos that took over Warburg and uses its rockets to threaten Paragon City. <br><br>Marshal Jason Blitz believed Lord Recluse wasn't acting fast enough in his bid to take over the world. He found it tragic that the Web had developed so many incredible weapons and none of them were being used on the hated heroes! <br><br>When Blitz learned he was dying of cancer, he decided to speed things up a bit so that he could live to see the defeat of Paragon City. He murdered Governor Melody Harkness and took over the city with a cadre of troops loyal to him. Soon after, he demolished the false façade on the Warburg Rocket at the centre of his city and started firing warheads armed with various toxins at Paragon City. <br><br>Lord Recluse promised the UN he would rectify the situation, but his troops have so far been stalemated by their rivals. (or so Recluse claims.)"
// DisplayClassName :
"P4289087208" "Marshal"
// DisplayNames :
"P2719249738" "Marshal Blitz"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Marshall_Blitz_Stage3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Arachnos_Flier_Mini 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1427654769" "Marshal Blitz's personal Flier has been miniaturized and equipped with stolen ordinance."
// DisplayNames :
"P489036201" "Blitzkrieg"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - RogueArachnos_Quad_Turret_Sig3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2550206939" "Rogue SAM Battery"

