// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Legionarii 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3846526210" "The Legionarii is the backbone to Romulus' army. Once they followed Imperious, but now through blackmail and a traitorous thirst for power, they have turned sides and bend their knee to Romulus."
// DisplayNames :
"P1055308494" "Legionarii"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Centurion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2593146201" "If the Legionarii were a spear, the Centurions would be the point. Sharpened to a deadly point, these men will do whatever it takes to cut down their enemies."
// DisplayNames :
"P759837164" "Centurion"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Centurion_Female 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2293155437" "If the Legionarii were a spear, the Centurions would be the point. Sharpened to a deadly point, these women will do whatever it takes to cut down their enemies."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Praefectus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2684350312" "Throughout the battlefield, you can hear the shouts and commands of the Praefectus. They alone can keep the bloodlust and battle frenzy that flows through the veins of every Cimeroran in check."
// DisplayNames :
"P1017901683" "Praefectus Castrorum"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Surgeon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P953137867" "The Surgeons have long been the healers among the Cimeroran. Even these few who have chosen to follow Romulus still wield the magical powers of their craft."
// DisplayNames :
"P3393000126" "Immunes Surgeon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Engineer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1232091453" "The tactics of the Engineer have been honed through countless battles. They function as a secondary team amongst the Centurions and Legionarii, performing quick strikes to the weakest points in their enemies armor."
// DisplayNames :
"P1247697609" "Immunes Engineer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Legatus_Legionis 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P1674388502" "Legatus Legionis"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Romulus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3306952828" "Once the right hand man to Imperious, Romulus turned traitor and overthrew Imperious. Now, Romulus sides with the Nictus and other more questionable forces to secure his tyrannical rule over Cimerora."
// DisplayNames :
"P3661135008" "Romulus Augustus"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Romulus_Nictus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P4051507704" "Romulus Augustus Nictus"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Cyclops 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P795552524" "Captured in the hills of Cimerora and brought to the gladiatorial pits, the Cyclops fights for no other purpose but to kill and maim. There are rumors that it has the blood of an Incarnate flowing through its veins, but none has claimed it as their own."
// DisplayNames :
"P3464002776" "Cyclops"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Minotaur 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P531633975" "The Minotaur is a beast of ancient times; born from the blood of a human and the passion of an Incarnate. Any man who dares challenge this beast will face a wrath of celestial force."
// DisplayNames :
"P2701362346" "Minotaur"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_NictusOrb_1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2229915464" "This energy enmity was formed when the life force from a defeated foe was infused with Nictus Energy."
// DisplayNames :
"P4223579157" "Nictus Essence"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_NictusOrb_2 
