// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Good_Praefectus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Good_Surgeon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3892378128" "The Surgeons have long been the healers among the Cimeroran. They have trained at their craft for most of their live seeking to aid those surrounding them."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Good_Engineer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Good_Daedalus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P990194006" "Daedalus is the finest crafter these ancient times have ever seen. His gift borders on Celestial, but is in fact simply his own genius at work."
// DisplayClassName :
"P4059873720" "Hero"
// DisplayNames :
"P2292978780" "Daedalus"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Good_Imperious 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3390862989" "Born from both Incarnate and Man, Imperious commands the forces of Justice against the armies of darkness. His Pantheon of heroes fight at his side without question. He is truly the leader of these people and the visionary of the future."
// DisplayNames :
"P1987342420" "Imperious"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Good_Sister_Sybil 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3214081717" "Sister Solaris is the matriarch of the Seers. She has the strongest connection to the Oracle and therefore the greatest ability to glean the futures of mankind."
// DisplayNames :
"P284457898" "Sister Solaris"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Good_Sybil_Bramlett 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2930732744" "Fortunata Bramlett has come to Cimerora and disguised herself as a Sybil to aid Sister Airlia's plans."
// DisplayClassName :
"P2290135600" "Villain"
// GroupDescription :
// DisplayNames :
"P2163801772" "Sybil Bramlett"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Good_Sister_Airlia 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P525884029" "Although an outcast from the community of Sybils, Sister Airlia nevertheless shows an amazing prescience for tasks that will help drive Romulus from the Cimerora Peninsula -- and that will increase her own power. Despite arguments from other members of Cimerora, Imperious has allowed Airlia back in to act as an advisor."
// DisplayClassName :
"P2166909532" "Prophet"
// DisplayNames :
"P4291176104" "Sister Airlia"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Romans_Good_Marcus_Valerius 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3899846390" "Marcus Valerius"

