// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4076795486" "This Misguided Citizen appears to be taking an interest in one of the magical cults that pervades First Ward."
// GroupDescription :
"P1063539622" "Doomsayer Cultists"
// DisplayNames :
"P1518653835" "Misguided Citizen"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Inciter 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3707439281" "This young woman has sworn her allegiance to the Talons of Vengeance, a powerful force of fanatical warriors who seek to punish those who have committed particulary egregious offenses of oathbreaking, betrayal and deceit. The Inciter remains mostly human, and is a swift, vicious opponent who favors moving in for deadly strikes with her imbued claws."
// DisplayClassName :
"P2703355240" "Underling"
// DisplayNames :
"P331643796" "Inciter"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Archer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P648478890" "This young woman has sworn her allegiance to the Talons of Vengeance, a powerful force of fanatical warriors who seek to punish those who have committed particulary egregious offenses of oathbreaking, betrayal and deceit. The Archer remains mostly human, and is a skilled archer with the means to ensnare her targets and then to quickly dispatch them with a barrage of arrows."
// DisplayNames :
"P1057130050" "Archer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Zealot 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1421586319" "This young woman has sworn her allegiance to the Talons of Vengeance, a powerful force of fanatical warriors who seek to punish those who have committed particulary egregious offenses of oathbreaking, betrayal and deceit. The Zealot remains mostly human, and is a swift, vicious opponent who favors moving in for deadly strikes with her imbued claws."
// DisplayNames :
"P979309152" "Zealot"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Huntress 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3905459956" "This young woman has sworn her allegiance to the Talons of Vengeance, a powerful force of fanatical warriors who seek to punish those who have committed particulary egregious offenses of oathbreaking, betrayal and deceit. The Huntress remains mostly human, and is a skilled archer with the means to ensnare her targets and then to quickly dispatch them with a barrage of arrows."
// DisplayNames :
"P1569897207" "Huntress"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Banshee 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2090502207" "The Banshee was once a woman with a melodic voice who died in the many battles waged in and around First Ward. Her gift in life has become a curse in death, twisted by the Talons of Vengeance into a terrifying harbinger of bad tidings. Through her otherworldly cries and shouts, the Banshee serves as a messenger of the torment the Talons bring to all those who have incurred their wrath."
// DisplayNames :
"P2974691618" "Banshee"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Reviler 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3859611982" "One of the more dramatic transformations caused by an allegiance to the Talons of Vengeance, the Reviler has lost almost all resemblance to her former human self. This woman has now become a humanoid bird with exceptional vision and the ability to fly. Because of her extremely keen senses and superior mobility, the Reviler makes an excellent scout and archer."
// DisplayNames :
"P2800724313" "Reviler"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Elementalist_Fire 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3385538929" "Having long ago sworn fealty to the Talons of Vengeance, the Elementalist has been twisted into a half-human, half-serpent monstrosities. In the process of transformation, however, they gain significant aptitude with the mystical elements, allowing them to call forth a variety of elementally attuned powers. In addition, they become more resistant to the element with which they have an affinity."
// DisplayNames :
"P30803198" "Elementalist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Elementalist_Ice 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Elementalist_Shadow 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Raider 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2555416154" "The Raiders are ferocious, intense fighters who have endured through the many tribulations a footsoldier of the Talons of Vengeance must face. They are fanatically loyal to their sisters and the cause of the Talons, seeking to sow the destruction which is meted out to those who have betrayed the principles of the Furies. They are dangerous opponents who can make quick work of a foe if they are allowed to approach too close."
// DisplayNames :
"P4222026277" "Raider"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Spiritualist_Fire 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P609079313" "Having long ago sworn fealty to the Talons of Vengeance, the Spiritualist has been twisted into a half-human, half-serpent monstrosities. In the process of transformation, however, they gain significant aptitude with the mystical elements, allowing them to call forth a variety of elementally attuned powers. In addition, they become more resistant to the element with which they have an affinity."
// DisplayNames :
"P1879536298" "Spiritualist"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Spiritualist_Ice 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Spiritualist_Shadow 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Fanatic 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3606083114" "The Fanatics have taken the intense devotion of the Zealots to another level. While still retaining the swift and deadly claw attacks of their lesser sisters, the Fanatics acquire new abilities, including the ability to call forth a poisonous energy that saps their targets of strength. They are dangerous opponents who can make quick work of a foe if they are allowed to approach too close."
// DisplayNames :
"P4026219016" "Fanatic"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Harpy 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P133556473" "One of the more dramatic transformations caused by an allegiance to the Talons of Vengeance, the Harpy has lost almost all resemblance to her former human self. This woman has now become a humanoid bird with exceptional vision and the ability to fly. Because of her extremely keen senses and superior mobility, the Harpy makes an excellent scout and archer."
// DisplayNames :
"P2091415715" "Harpy"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Lamia 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2170208703" "The Lamia was once a swift warrior who excelled in hand to hand combat with claw weapons. Through her allegiance to the Talons of Vengeance, she has been morphed into a fast-moving half-serpent, able to close rapidly with her foes to deliver vicious attacks without mercy."
// DisplayNames :
"P373164896" "Lamia"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Prophetess_Fire 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2935973023" "The Prophetesses were once women who held a latent connection to the mystical elements. Rather than be twisted into a half-serpent monstrosity like their lesser kin, for whom elemental affinity was not natural, the Prophetesses retain much of their human form, with only their skin and feet showing the changes they have undergone as members of the Talons of Vengeance. They have a much greater control over the elements to which they are attuned and are capable of quickly overwhelming the unprepared with a flood of mystical energy in the form of fire, ice, shadow, lightning or earth."
// DisplayNames :
"P3007457000" "Prophetess"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Prophetess_Ice 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Prophetess_Shadow 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Prophetess_Lightning 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Prophetess_Earth 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Disciple 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P250832457" "The Disciples are extremely loyal members of the Talons whose bodies have been deformed in a more avian fashion than others of the group, with feathered wings sprouting from their backs. They are elite hunters, with tremendous talent as archers. Like their bow-wielding sisters, they can ensnare their targets. However, their greater skill and attunement to the mystical arts has given them the ability to shoot arrows of fire and ice."
// DisplayNames :
"P1672481055" "Disciple"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Oracle_Fire 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P534666929" "The Oracles were once women who held a latent connection to the mystical elements. Rather than be twisted into a half-serpent monstrosity like the Spiritualists, for whom elemental affinity was not natural, the Oracles retain much of their human form, with only their skin and feet showing the changes they have undergone as members of the Talons of Vengeance. They have a much greater control over the elements to which they are attuned and are capable of quickly overwhelming the unprepared with a flood of mystical energy in the form of earth, fire, ice, shadow or lightning."
// DisplayNames :
"P4047896278" "Oracle"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Oracle_Ice 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Oracle_Shadow 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Oracle_Lightning 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Oracle_Earth 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Devotee 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2548065489" "The Devotees are extremely loyal members of the Talons whose bodies have been deformed in a more avian fashion than others of the group, with feathered wings sprouting from their backs. They are elite hunters, with tremendous talent as archers. Like the Huntresses, they can ensnare their targets. However, their greater skill and attunement to the mystical arts has given them the ability to shoot arrows of fire and ice."
// DisplayNames :
"P376187006" "Devotee"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Siren 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P834609738" "The Siren was once a woman whose voice was so alluring that she could enrapture anyone she met through the power of speech or song. In swearing her allegiance to the Talons of Vengeance, this woman was blessed with new strength in her voice, enabling her to control and influence those around her even more effectively. There is a great darkness hidden within her songs, however, for her only goal is to lure the unwary to their doom in the name of exacting the terrible vengance demanded by the Talons."
// DisplayNames :
"P441095436" "Siren"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Gorgon_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3689216767" "The Gorgons are among the most monstrous members of the Talons of Vengeance. They are fully transformed hybrids between woman and serpent, with almost no trace of the person they once were emerging from their hideous faces. They are extremely powerful swordswomen, capable of cutting through their enemies with speed and precision. Worse still, they make full use of their terrifying appearance to control their enemies, even to the point of turning them to stone."
// DisplayNames :
"P2084369774" "Gorgon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Harridan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1408337459" "The Harridan are among the most monstrous members of the Talons of Vengeance. They are fully transformed hybrids between woman and serpent, with almost no trace of the person they once were emerging from their hideous faces. They are extremely powerful swordswomen, capable of cutting through their enemies with speed and precision. Worse still, they make full use of their terrifying appearance to control their enemies, even to the point of turning them to stone."
// DisplayNames :
"P2826933193" "Harridan"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Sibyl_Fire 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3815813283" "Sibyls are women whose mastery of a single element has given them great capacity for bending the world around them to their will. So concentrated is their power that rare natural events become their playthings. Very few members of the Talons have the inner strength to endure the training needed for such mastery, which makes those who survive the ordeal capable of defending strongly against attacks of their own element. These women have sprouted powerful wings, enabling them to sow destruction over a far greater territory than their lesser sisters. The Sibyl is also wreathed in a continuous aura of energy formed of their element, as though their bodies are forever moments away from becoming pure elemental energy."
// DisplayNames :
"P236259853" "Sibyl"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Sibyl_Ice 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Sibyl_Shadow 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Sibyl_Lightning 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Sibyl_Earth 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Diviner 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1715701921" "One of the chosen few who trained in the specialized magics used by Sorceress Serene, the Diviner has mastered the elemental spirit of the autumn, bringing the fury of fire and the weight of ice to her opponents in unique combination attacks. Whether wielding blades of fire and ice or casting magical spells which share in the power of both elements, the Diviner is a force of nature who aims to bring swift death to all who oppose her."
// DisplayNames :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Gorgon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Sorceress 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4251314594" "One of the chosen few who trained in the specialized magics used by Sorceress Serene, the Sorceress has mastered the elemental spirit of the autumn, bringing the fury of fire and the weight of ice to her opponents in unique combination attacks. Whether wielding blades of fire and ice or casting magical spells which share in the power of both elements, the Sorceress is a force of nature who aims to bring swift death to all who oppose her."
// DisplayNames :
"P1114436782" "Sorceress"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Keres 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1157689132" "The Keres is among the oldest and most loyal of all the members of the Talons of Vengeance, having ascended to her current state through the blessing of the Furies themselves. She has been tasked with being a walking engine of death and destruction. She channels the bitter energy of death through all of her attacks, making her already ferocious skill with her titanic axe even more deadly. These vicious combatants are walking embodiments of the inevitability of death to those who cross the Furies."
// DisplayNames :
"P1661639214" "Keres"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Sorceress_Serene 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P609942659" "Even when she was a young woman, Clarissa Moore was clearly a powerful mystic. Back then she was much more open and forgiving. She felt safe and hopeful for a bright future when she was taken in and taught the wonders of elemental magic by her coven. They became her family.  When Diabolique slaughtered them all, Clarissa barely escaped the same fate. She was nursing her wounds when the Furies found her and gave her a new kind of hope... the hope for revenge. Since Diabolique is allied with Tyrant, Clarissa is a focused and uncompromising ally in the Furies war against Marcus Cole and all those who serve him."
// DisplayNames :
"P886910818" "Sorceress Serene"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Sorceress_Serene_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P443060137" "This flickering image is merely a projection of the evil Sorceress Serene. It is but a shadow of her true power."
// DisplayNames :
"P852714917" "Projection of Sorceress Serene"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Sorceress_Serene_Spirit 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1827729464" "Sorceress Serene's undying spirit has lost none of its potency despite lacking a physical body. In fact, her rage and anger at her untimely death has only strengthened her powers."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Sorceress_Serene_Boss_WarWitch 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P144801717" "The body of Sorceress Serene has been claimed by the spirit of War Witch instead."
// DisplayNames :
"P41739984" "War Witch"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - TalonsOfVengeance_Lamashtu 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2905794342" "Lamashtu is the daughter of Anu, the Sky God. Rather than follow the will of the gods, Lamashtu's malevolence knows no bounds. Left unchecked she threatens to consume and destroy all life. It is for these reasons that Lamashtu was sealed within the Eternal Prison by the gods and the Furies centuries ago. She bears seven names and when called upon in incantations she manifests as seven witches. She is responsible for many of the woes of ancient times. Nightmares, death, plague, sickness, and the wholesale slaughter of men, women, children along with feasting on their blood and bones are all grisly examples of her work. Lamashtu has an enduring hatred for all of creation. It is not surprising then, that she is the mother of all monsters, including those first corrupt creatures which would one day be claimed as servants of the Furies."
// DisplayNames :
"P1922801992" "Lamashtu"

