// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Low_Brawling_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2889186436" "The Trolls have abused their bodies with a particularly dangerous drug called Superadine. It has begun to literally turn them into monsters. These low ranking gang members aren't showing many signs of changing, but that doesn't stop them from acting like beasts."
// DisplayNames :
"P772368426" "Trollkin Brawler"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Low_Boxing_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P483761545" "Trollkin Bruiser"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Low_Bat_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P525342087" "Trollkin Slugger"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Low_Sledgehammer_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P3894034807" "Trollkin Slammer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Low_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2726707331" "After enough abuse of the dangerous drug called Superadine, A Troll will start to show some body-changing effects.  These Brutes are starting to develop superior strength and power, although nothing like their more veteran kin."
// DisplayNames :
"P3818541122" "Jutal"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Boxing_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3676389833" "The Trolls have abused their bodies with a particularly dangerous drug called Superadine. It has begun to literally turn them into monsters. These low ranking gang members are already showing signs of changing, but they still sometimes rely on conventional weapons."
// DisplayNames :
"P1231495341" "Trollkin Gunner"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Shotgun_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2353973142" "Trollkin Buckshot"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_SubmachineGun_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2514280209" "Veteran Trolls have been around long enough to feel some positive effects from their body-changing drugs. Like the trolls of legend, they have become exceptionally fast healers, making them very difficult to kill."
// DisplayNames :
"P468378595" "Gardvord"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Ogre_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3097334732" "The leaders of the Trolls have developed truly superhuman abilities. Not only do they heal fast and resist a variety of damage types, they're also capable of feats of tremendous strength. As a result, they have no need for weapons of any kind."
// DisplayNames :
"P2407187569" "Ogre"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Caliban_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2893301591" "Caliban"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Atta 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P314102864" "Leadership within the Trolls is determined largely based on a never-ending game of King of the Hill. The fearsome Atta won his position by defeating seven of the Trolls' former leaders in combat, mortally wounding three of them. Since that day, many Trolls have tried to dethrone him, but none have yet succeeded."
// DisplayNames :
"P552783348" "Atta"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Rundum 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Nictus_Hunter_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P52514483" "Trollkin Quantum Gunner"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Nictus_Hunter_Lieutenant 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P2432257318" "Gardvord Quantum"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Nictus_Hunter_Caliban_Boss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayNames :
"P4096442673" "Caliban Quantum"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - Trolls_Rave_Boxing_Thug 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2625486439" "These Trolls have managed to hit upon a stash of uncut Superadine. It's got them raging out of control and bent on destruction."

